WEBVTT

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.100
Smiling is so hard.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.340
No, it's true.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.820
Seriously?

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.450
<i>They're very energetic this morning.</i>

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.960
G-Good morning!

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.370
Good morning...

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.750
<i>I scare students just by looking at them.</i>

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.810
Kuzehashi-sensei!

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.970
Good mornin'!

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.770
Kujou-san, good—

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.170
Sensei, can I borrow your scrunchie?

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.850
Scrunchie! Your scrunchie!

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.640
Hurry! Hurry up!

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:10.890
H-Here.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.100
Thanks muchly!

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.780
Do you see this?

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:15.230
What?

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.450
Wh-What are you doing?

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:22.850
We're...

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.190
playing color tag!

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:26.600
Give that back.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.920
Present For You

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.250
Kujou-san's friendliness is a virtue,
but she needs to learn some restraint.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.140
Good morning, Kuzehashi-sensei.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.160
Good morning.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.040
U-Um, Karasuma-sensei...

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.670
This is for you. Please take it.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.000
For me?

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.590
Glee

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.010
It's so cute.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.730
Thank you very much.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.810
It's so soft.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:25.030
I actually have a favor to ask of you.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.130
Cuddle, cuddle... You're so cuddly.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:29.160
How can I get people to like me?

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:31.230
How are you so cuddly?

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:30.760
What?

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:33.160
What?

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.160
She just did that now

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.160
She just did that now...

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.160
So cuddly...

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.540
I see.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:39.180
You want your students
to stop fearing you, huh?

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.390
Yes.

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:41.450
Don't worry about it.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.120
You're great just the way you are.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.800
No, now that a new year has begun,
I'm trying to become a new person.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.400
<i>This year, my students will like me.</i>

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:54.810
<i>That's Matsubara-san and
Higurashi-san, from my class.</i>

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.440
<i>The morning assembly's about to start...</i>

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.640
Be sure to pat it a few times.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:08.140
<i>Again? Why?</i>

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.630
Sensei?

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:14.740
I'll collect your post-graduation plans now.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.960
Pass your forms forward.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.670
<i>Maybe it looked like I was glaring at them.</i>

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:24.890
<i>I should start wearing sunglasses...</i>

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.380
<i>No, that would be even scarier.</i>

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.330
<i>Kujou-san's smiling!</i>

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.310
<i>I need to respond somehow...</i>

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.520
Has Karen done something again?

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.470
<i>I did it again...</i>

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.920
Are you feeling down?

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:52.740
Sensei...

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.880
When you're feeling down,
you should squeeze something cute.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.160
Something cute?

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.870
Karasuma-sensei, you forgot something.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.920
Oh, thank you, Alice-san.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.560
Do you have a moment?

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.170
Huh?

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.300
Squeeze!

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.300
What?

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.310
<i>She just moved in and did it!</i>

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:11.680
Lucky

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.680
<i>Is she a god?</i>

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.380
Welcome back.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:16.680
What's wrong, Alice?

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.380
Karasuma-sensei squeezed me.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.940
Oh, I see.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.710
Squeeze!

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.080
Why would you do that?

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.070
Just because.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.320
Just because?!

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:28.320
Alice!

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.650
Alice is so cute when she's flustered.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:33.410
So are you, Ayaya!

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:38.160
Youko, please!

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.200
You too, Aya?

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.110
Shino, I finally get to see you!

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.090
Alice!

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.690
We've only had the morning assembly so far.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.980
Want to come to the library, Youko?

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.160
We're just going to return some books.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:59.310
Sure.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:00.560
Library

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.610
Blonde hair...

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:07.690
It must be hard to wash.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:08.650
Japanese
Dictionary

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.320
Karen, are you familiar with the
Japanese expression "grinding sesame"?

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.070
It means humoring someone
so they'll like you.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.120
Yes, just like that.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.930
Sesame garnish, sesame
sauce, sesame ice cream.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:23.230
Japanese people love sesame.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.080
And it's good for you, too.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.830
Sesame, huh?

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.240
I see you're both studying hard.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:35.130
By the way, Karen, you've been
trying to become friends with

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.220
Kuzehashi-sensei recently, haven't you?

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:39.770
Yeah. I want to be friends with her.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:41.150
I know!

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:44.340
Since Japanese people love it so much,
I'll give her some sesame.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.850
I'm sure she'd like it a lot.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:47.760
You're really grinding that sesame!

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:49.270
Roasted Sesame

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.900
This is for you.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:51.900
Sesame...

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:55.070
Th-Thank you very much, Kujou-san...

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:00.600
Have some coffee.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.370
Karasuma-sensei.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:03.550
Yes?

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.630
I don't understand my students.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:10.880
Next weekend, I'm holding

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.510
a tea party at my house.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:15.020
A party?

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:16.730
It's an afternoon tea party.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.350
Shino's really into it right now.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:22.770
Afternoon tea is a tea party held
around four in the afternoon.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:26.380
English noblewomen began
holding afternoon tea parties

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.940
in the mid-19th century as social events.

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:31.140
Tea is very English.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:32.650
Aren't you a little late to the party?

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:36.300
I actually didn't realize
black tea was so popular.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.340
Because...

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.230
Alice never drinks it!

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.910
Fuuu~

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:41.780
Nothing beats green tea.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:43.910
I like black tea, too.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.600
Is tea all you have during afternoon tea?

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:47.580
Youko...

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:50.200
I mean, I was hoping there'd be snacks.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.260
Of course there will be.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.450
But I want to make it a proper tea party.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.840
What are you going to do?

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:58.950
Make sweets!

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.680
Sounds nice. Normally,
you'd make scones, though.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.950
Ooh, me! I want cookies!

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.690
Let's make some of those, too.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:09.590
All right! I'm so excited!

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:10.810
You're going to make both?

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:13.480
Will you be okay? Isn't that a bit too greedy?

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:20.370
Rumble

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.750
You should listen to your desires!

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:18.740
I'm putting my life on the
line for this tea party!

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:20.370
Why would you go that far?

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:27.210
Smells nice.

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:33.710
Sesame is delicious, isn't it?

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:35.700
Ground sesame is even tastier.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:36.840
I agree.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:39.970
It has more calories than roasted
sesame, but I prefer it, too.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.410
Sensei?

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.850
C-Calories?

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:49.850
Coming!

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:52.480
Thank you for coming.

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:53.930
Thanks for inviting us.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:54.990
Pardon the intrusion.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:56.740
We've already got everything ready.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:59.700
Okay! Let's get started.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:01.690
You're baking in those clothes?

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.120
They'll get dirty.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.630
A maid must always wear her uniform.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:08.410
It's okay. I'll be careful.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.890
Told you so.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:15.840
I'm glad it didn't stain.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:16.760
Yeah...

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.110
Thank you.

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:19.620
Hey, where's Karen?

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.930
She said she'd be late.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:24.050
She's bringing us a cake stand.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.310
Really?

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:26.660
How authentic.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.600
Karen, welcome—

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.940
Pardon the intrusion.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:37.500
Karen! That's not a cake stand!

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.070
That's a food delivery box!

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:41.610
The cake stand was heavy,
so I brought something similar.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:44.930
You put the food in here.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:46.980
It's not similar!

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:48.830
They're nothing alike!

00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:53.470
There, there. It's fine as long
as we can put stuff in it.

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:56.250
Let's pull ourselves together
and make some sweets.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:01.980
You're the only one with real cooking
experience, so I'm counting on you.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:04.680
I haven't really baked much before...

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:06.220
I'm counting on you!

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:08.060
We're counting on you!

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:10.600
Stop that! I don't do well under pressure!

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:16.320
I wonder if Kuzehashi-sensei's a good cook.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:17.780
I bet she's great at it.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.820
She teaches home ec.

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:22.670
What are you making?

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:23.480
Onee-chan.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:24.320
Isa-nee.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.620
We're making cookies and scones.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.540
Do you have the day off?

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.550
Yeah.

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:32.200
I know. Why don't we get Isa-nee to help us?

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:35.170
Good idea. I'm a little uneasy
about doing it by ourselves.

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:36.250
Sure.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.920
Incidentally, my best dish is fried eggs.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.450
Burnt to a crisp.

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:43.590
Never mind, then.

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:46.090
Let me know when they're done.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.990
I'm not great at delicate tasks like these...

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.230
Sorry!

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.860
Cake Flour

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:02.840
You're so clumsy, Youko.

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.080
Sorry, Aya. Are you okay?

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:08.850
Jeez, Youko! Just go and sit down!

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.370
I'll do everything!

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:11.670
Sorry...

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.960
Normally, it's the other way around.

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:19.960
The sun is setting. What should we do?

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.590
How many hours have we been baking?

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.680
It's not really afternoon tea anymore.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:27.590
What?!

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.100
Assam! Darjeeling! Earl Grey!

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.040
Shino, calm down!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.310
Pick up the pace, everyone!

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:36.460
We can still make it!

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.480
This is one frantic tea party!

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:40.580
There.

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:45.050
Now we just have to cut out
the cookies and bake them.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.320
I brought a bunch of cookie cutters.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.480
They're all hearts.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.710
They're cute, but they're all the same.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.890
Karen, yours have sesame in them.

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:02.250
They're sesame cookies.

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:08.550
<i>It's a mass production of hearts...</i>

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:10.390
<i>Hearts...</i>

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.640
What's wrong with you?!

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:21.140
It's so boring when they're all the same!

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:23.070
Hurry it up, you two!

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.190
They're done!

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:47.570
Hooray!

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:48.000
They look delicious!

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:48.950
Yeah!

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.850
They look great!

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:51.770
But it's nighttime...

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.180
Pitch Black

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.350
It's all about how you feel inside!

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:56.910
Let's make some tea!

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.670
It's time for dinner.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.520
You can have your tea party tomorrow.

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:06.620
The cookies are so crispy.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:08.400
They're just sweet enough, too.

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:10.610
The mood is ruined, though.

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:11.320
You think so?

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:14.490
As long as we're eating together,
we can have fun anywhere.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:16.320
Alice...

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:18.050
You're right.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:21.940
But next time, let's have tea at your place.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:23.560
When are you free?

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:25.380
<i>She's determined!</i>

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:27.520
Thanks for the food.

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:28.730
You're finished?

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:29.260
Yes.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.430
I'm going to go share some around.

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:33.100
Here you go.

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.750
Thanks for always giving me snacks.

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:37.080
These are all for us?

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.100
Thanks.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.100
You're welcome.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:41.560
Here you go.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:43.560
For me?

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:46.200
We made these cookies yesterday.

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.860
Please share them with the other teachers.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.200
Th-Thank you.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:51.820
You're welcome.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:54.950
Sesame

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:56.940
Sesame again?!

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:00.460
Is she trying to tell me something?

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.290
I figured it out.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:04.430
And?

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.910
Sesame must be the in-thing
for high school girls right now.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:09.630
Huh?

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:12.150
Keeping up with the latest trends

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:14.340
Smug

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:14.340
will help you understand your students.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.190
I see.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:17.470
That's very informative.

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:19.990
Sesame!

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:22.690
Open sesame.

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:26.280
Hello, everyone.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.190
Open sesame.

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:34.320
Open sesame!

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:41.080
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.620
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.830
Faculty Office

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:50.100
You're making happi coats in home ec today?

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:51.880
That sounds fun.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.080
These hands-on lessons
make me nervous, though.

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:57.560
You'll be okay. With a little spirit,
you can get through it.

00:14:57.860 --> 00:14:59.090
For example...

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.850
Happis make me happy!

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:04.340
You can't fail if you open with that.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.780
B-But...

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:08.020
<i>She's got nothing but spirit...</i>

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:11.350
I'm sure they'll all roar with laughter.

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:14.600
I'm so excited to make happi coats.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:17.150
Your class has home ec for fifth period, right?

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:19.650
Yeah, and yours is tomorrow.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.550
Yeah! I want to make mine soon!

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:25.490
Aya-chan, you can make
them any size you want.

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:27.910
You don't need to take measurements.

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:29.660
I-I know that.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:32.500
I was just seeing how much
Youko has grown in the last year.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:33.420
How much have I grown?

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:36.580
It's great that you're so full of energy!

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.420
That has nothing to do
with my measurements.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:41.910
I'd rather have a cooking lesson.

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:45.180
I've been into sewing lately,
so I'm happy we're doing this.

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:46.510
You're into a lot of things.

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:50.610
Cute clothes and accessories
can be so expensive.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.220
Like this

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:53.690
I try to make everything I can myself.

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:55.120
That's amazing!

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:57.520
You made this yourself?
What an unexpected talent...

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.930
It must be because you love foreign stuff.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.280
With this much passion,

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:05.030
you might actually become
an interpreter someday.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:07.980
And ultimately, you'll become a
hero the whole world will know!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.400
What?!

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.290
Historical Figure

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.290
Shino's amazing!

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:10.320
Sewing Room

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:14.290
<i>It's Karasuma-sensei's advice...</i>

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:16.000
<i>I'll trust her.</i>

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:19.820
Happi... Happy... Happy...

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:21.650
Kuzehashi-sensei!

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:24.420
I'm really excited about today's class!

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:27.680
Happis make me happy!

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:30.180
Just kidding.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:31.750
Kujou-san!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.800
Wh-Why are you mad at me?!

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:34.730
I'm Sorry!

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.190
Happi

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:38.660
If you have any questions, just ask.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:41.440
There are sewing machines
in the sewing room,

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:43.690
and all kinds of dangerous equipment.

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:47.200
I'm sure you know what will
happen if you play around.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.260
Okay, begin!

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:52.450
(Translation) Be careful
you don't hurt yourselves!

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:52.070
<i>Be careful you don't hurt yourselves!</i>

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.280
Alone

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:56.620
<i>Feel free to ask me any questions...</i>

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:58.070
Sensei.

00:16:58.070 --> 00:16:58.710
Yes?

00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:00.460
Do you have a question?

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:01.960
I'm finished.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:02.590
What?

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:06.840
O-Oomiya-san! Is that really you, Oomiya-san?

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:09.100
This is wonderful.

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:11.100
The stitching is extremely precise.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:14.660
I'm glad you did such a thorough job.

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:16.100
What is it?

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:19.710
I'm happy that you praised me.

00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:21.610
Th-That's...

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.490
Aya-chan, how's yours coming?

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.610
It keeps going off center.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:36.400
You need to go faster.

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:37.520
B-But...

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:40.120
I'm afraid of the needle!

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:40.960
It's okay.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.280
It's okay!

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:45.010
Imagine you're jumping off
the stage at Kiyomizu!

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:47.380
This takes that much resolve?!

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:52.160
Take a ten minute break.

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:52.640
Another hour, huh?

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:55.640
<i>Kujou-san, it's break time...</i>

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:58.580
Karen, what are you making?

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:01.150
I'm making a doll out of my leftover cloth.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.340
<i>Is it for the girl in Class C?</i>

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:10.390
Alice, what's that on your head?

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:12.120
A bride's veil.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:14.140
Shino made it for me.

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:16.540
She said I look good in white,

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:19.140
so she wants to make a
wedding dress for me someday.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:20.410
Really?

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:23.160
In Japan, they say that if you wear a
wedding dress before the big day,

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.170
you'll delay your own wedding.

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:27.800
Do they say that abroad?

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:29.730
What? You don't want it?

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:32.230
But it looks so good on you...

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.010
Happi

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.010
Continued

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:35.560
Kujou-san.

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:36.260
Yes?

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:40.850
If you have any questions, you can ask me.

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:42.500
Thank you.

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:43.400
But...

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:47.530
Enter
Karen

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:45.880
Shino helped me finish mine.

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:47.530
Sun

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:47.580
I'm finished, too.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:49.290
Why are there words on them?

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:50.710
To express our individuality.

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:57.330
If you didn't finish your happi today,
finish it by our next class.

00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:58.220
Goodbye.

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:01.640
<i>Today didn't go so well, either.</i>

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:02.970
Kuzehashi-sensei!

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:05.630
This is for you.

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:07.780
The thing you were making earlier...

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:12.370
Kujou-san, you keep giving me gifts.

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:14.170
Is there something you want from me?

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.560
You have a beautiful smile.

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:17.140
What?

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:19.600
I want to see you smile more.

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:21.780
Kujou-san...

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:33.260
<i>Am I imagining things?
I thought I saw something...</i>

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:37.930
I accept your gift.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:39.620
Okay.

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:47.810
Thank you.

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:51.210
Faculty Office

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:50.510
Excuse me.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:52.970
Thanks for waiting.

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:55.150
Everyone's waiting at the entrance.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:01.240
Goodbye, Karasu-chan and Kusshi-chan.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:04.170
You're being too familiar with the teachers!

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:07.020
I prefer calling people by nicknames.

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:12.440
As long as you're sensible about it,
I don't care what you call me.

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:15.910
Kuzehashi-sensei!

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:17.700
See you tomorrow.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:25.710
Kusshi sounds a bit like cookie, doesn't it?

00:20:25.710 --> 00:20:27.790
Which is fine. It's easy to say,

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:30.210
and you can't choose your own nickname...

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:34.410
Hey! What is it, Sensei?

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:36.060
I'm sorry...

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:38.150
I-I'm not saying...

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:42.650
Good morning.

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:44.220
Good morning.

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:48.600
Kuzehashi-sensei's been more
cheerful and easier to talk to lately.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:49.980
She's so cute when she smiles.

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:53.710
I understand Kuzehashi-sensei
a little better now.

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:54.420
Me, too.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.370
She's every bit as nice as Karasuma-sensei.

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:02.010
I'm glad everyone finally realized it.

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:01.330
Smug

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:03.870
Why do you sound so smug?

00:21:04.100 --> 00:21:06.700
Sensei and I are already friends.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.640
I can even dance with her.

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.390
Maybe you shouldn't...

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:09.710
Watch this.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:11.780
Kuzehashi-sensei!

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:13.680
Let's dance!

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:14.440
What?

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.630
Anyway, where's your homework?

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:18.120
What? Um...

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:20.560
You <i>did</i> do your homework, didn't you?

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:22.210
Hold it!

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:24.190
Are they really friends?

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:25.160
You know what they say:

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:27.600
The more difficult a student is,
the more endearing they are.

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:29.570
You won't get away with this!

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.060
I'm sorry!

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:31.060
Sorry isn't good enough!

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:02.820
If you were an animal...

00:23:03.710 --> 00:23:05.370
Karen-san would be a cat.

00:23:05.370 --> 00:23:07.160
Komichi-san would be a black rabbit.

00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:09.180
Karasu-chan, what would I be?

00:23:09.560 --> 00:23:11.160
Inokuma-san, you'd be...

00:23:12.650 --> 00:23:14.670
Since you eat everything in sight, you'd be...

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:17.090
Vroooo

00:23:14.970 --> 00:23:15.700
a vacuum cleaner.

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:17.090
At least pick an actual animal!

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:18.390
I see it.

00:23:18.390 --> 00:23:20.510
Karasu-chan, don't agree with her!

00:23:21.010 --> 00:23:24.840
Ballroom
Dancing

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:23.880
Kujou-san invited me to dance with her...

00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:24.050
Studying

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:24.840
Oh my

00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:24.840
Oh my...

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:27.890
1
Week
Later

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:26.800
We can dance now.

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.320
What are you talking about?

00:23:26.890 --> 00:23:27.890
Forgot

00:23:28.320 --> 00:23:29.820
That's not how the steps go!

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:30.630
It's like this!

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:33.180
Like
this

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:32.200
No!

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:33.180
She's so serious.

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:34.470
See you!

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:35.560
You're So Bright

00:23:34.470 --> 00:23:35.560
Wait!
